+      "solution": "I built, debugged, and verified a complete solution. The full self-contained markdown is at **`~/hygienic-incremental-macro-expander/SOLUTION.md`** (1032 lines). I verified it by extracting its embedded code blocks into a clean directory and re-running them: **12/12 checks pass**.\n\n## What the diagnosis found\n\nThe failure class has five independent root causes; four are standard, one is the subtle killer:\n\n1. **Global-gensym renaming** is neither hygienic (a macro temp can capture a user argument) nor stable (a global counter renumbers everything after an unrelated edit, invalidating caches).\n2. **Caching by spelling** instead of resolved binding identity lets an unrelated edit capture a reused expansion.\n3. **Over-broad invalidation** (re-expanding the whole module) defeats incrementality and perturbs generated scopes.\n4. **Lost source locations** because templates are built without `loc`.\n5. **Lexical scopes applied after macro expansion** — the bug that survives fixes 1–4. If you expand first and then assign lexical scopes, a macro-introduced free identifier receives the *use-site* scope, so subset resolution lets a local binder capture it:\n   ```scheme\n   (define-syntax use-helper (syntax-rules () ((_ x) (helper x))))\n   (let ((helper 42)) (use-helper 5))   ; naive post-pass: helper binds to the local!\n   ```\n\n## The exact fix\n\nA **scope-set** model (Flatt's *Binding as Sets of Scopes*) with strict ordering:\n\n- Binding forms (`lambda`/`let`) add a fresh lexical scope to binder + body.\n- Each macro expansion adds a fresh macro scope **only to template-origin syntax**; arguments are cloned untouched.\n- A reference binds to the largest scope set that is a subset of the reference's scopes.\n- Scopes come from a counter **reset per top-level form**, making expansion reproducible and cache-stable.\n- **Expansion and resolution run in one pass** (`process`), so lexical scopes are applied to the raw use before the macro fires. This is what makes `use-helper` stay free.\n- Cache validity = source hash + hashes of every macro/top-level value actually used; reverse dependency edges give the smallest sound recomputation region.\n- Introduced nodes inherit the macro-use `loc`; arguments keep theirs.\n\nKey excerpt (full file in `SOLUTION.md`):\n\n```js\nfunction process(node, env, macroEnv, ctx) {\n  if (node.type === 'symbol') { /* resolve by largest subset */ }\n  const head = node.items[0];\n  if (head && head.type === 'symbol') {\n    if (macroEnv.has(head.name)) {\n      const macro = macroEnv.get(head.name);\n      for (const rule of macro.rules) {\n        const binds = match(rule.pattern, node, macro.literals, {});\n        if (binds) {\n          ctx.usedMacros.add(macro.name);\n          const scope = ctx.freshScope();\n          // template gets `scope`; substituted args do not\n          const inst = instantiate(rule.template, binds, scope, node.loc);\n          return process(inst, env, macroEnv, ctx);   // reassign result!\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    if (head.name === 'let') {\n      const lex = ctx.freshLex();\n      // ...add lex to binders, then to raw body BEFORE recursing...\n      for (let i = 2; i < node.items.length; i++)\n        node.items[i] = process(node.items[i], env.concat(added), macroEnv, ctx);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ncd ~/hygienic-incremental-macro-expander\nnode test.js\n```\n\n```\n12 checks passed\n```\n\nCovers: hygiene/no-capture of a macro temp, definition-site free identifiers, nested-scope shadowing, mutually recursive macros (`my-even?`/`my-odd?`), smallest sound recomputation region, unrelated-edit reuse, cache-capture safety, determinism, source-location preservation, cross-expansion distinct temp bindings, and transitive `B → A → C → user` invalidation with independent forms reused.\n\n**Deliverables:** `SOLUTION.md` (title, root-cause analysis, full code, verification), plus the runnable `macro-expander.js` and `test.js`.\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: hygienic-incremental-macro-expansion\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-10-06T04:06:46.189Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
